---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { services, proof, findings } from "../data/services";
---

<Layout
  title="17th Street Labs | We break AI systems. Then we make them hold."
  description="A founder-led AI engineering and security firm in Denver. We build agentic products, attack them before anyone else can, and prove they work with real evaluations."
>
  <section class="hero ground-blue">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">17th Street Labs, Denver. AI engineering, evals, and security.</p>
      <h1 class="statement">We break AI systems.<br />Then we make them hold.</h1>
      <div class="hero-bottom">
        <p class="lede">
          Two founders, twenty-five years deep, for teams shipping agents that
          touch real data, real money, and real people. We build the product,
          attack it before anyone else can, and prove it works with numbers you
          can defend.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/contact/" data-contact-dialog class="button button-solid">
            Bring us the hard problem
          </a>
          <a class="button button-line" href="/services/"><span>What we do</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ticker" aria-label={`Failure modes we keep finding: ${findings.join(", ")}`}>
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="ticker-head">Failure modes we keep finding</span>
        <span class="ticker-track" aria-hidden="true">
          {[...findings, ...findings].map((item) => (
            <span>{item}</span>
          ))}
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band ground-white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <dl class="proof">
        {proof.map(({ value, label }) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{value}</dt>
            <dd>{label}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band ground-black">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 class="section-title">What we do</h2>
        <p>
          Four ways in. Most engagements start with one and grow into another
          once the first result lands.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="index">
        {services.map((service) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/services/#${service.slug}`}>
              <h3>{service.title}</h3>
              <div class="index-body">
                <p>{service.summary}</p>
                <span class="outcome">{service.outcome}</span>
              </div>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band ground-grey">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 class="section-title">Work you can inspect</h2>
        <p>We publish our research so you can judge our thinking before you hire us.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="research">
        <div>
          <h3 class="research-title">Exploit<br />Hunter</h3>
          <p class="lede">
            An open-source, local-first lab for studying how AI models discover,
            validate, and report security findings across long-running attack
            workflows. It is also the evaluation harness we use on client work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dl class="stats">
            <div><dt>412M+</dt><dd>tokens evaluated</dd></div>
            <div><dt>173</dt><dd>model profiles compared</dd></div>
            <div><dt>4,835</dt><dd>scored evaluation rows</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <ul class="marks">
            <li>Deterministic and LLM judges scored side by side</li>
            <li>Trajectory, evidence, cost, and tool telemetry on every run</li>
            <li>Reproducible regression gates you can put in CI</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://exploithunter.app" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Explore ExploitHunter
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band ground-white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 class="section-title">How an engagement starts</h2>
        <p>Three steps, in this order. No discovery theater.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Frame the question that matters</h3>
          <div>
            <p>
              We name the decision, failure mode, or capability at stake and
              agree on what success looks like before anyone writes code.
            </p>
            <p class="n">Usually one to two weeks, fixed fee, written recommendation.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Build the smallest credible proof</h3>
          <div>
            <p>
              Architecture, research, and evaluation move together so evidence
              arrives early enough to change direction cheaply.
            </p>
            <p class="n">Working software and measured results, not a deck.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Harden what survives, then hand it over</h3>
          <div>
            <p>
              We pressure-test the system, turn findings into controls, and
              leave your team able to run it without us.
            </p>
            <p class="n">The goal is that you do not need us for the next change.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band ground-grey">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 class="section-title">Who you work with</h2>
        <p>The people you meet are the people who do the work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="founders">
        <div class="founder">
          <h3>Dan Levy</h3>
          <p class="role">Co-founder, principal AI engineer</p>
          <p class="bio">
            Twenty-five years across production systems, developer platforms,
            AI applications, evaluation infrastructure, and offensive and
            defensive AI security. Grew one platform org from six engineers to
            sixty. Still writes the code on every engagement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="founder">
          <h3>Marina Levy</h3>
          <p class="role">Co-founder, chief executive</p>
          <p class="bio">
            Runs the firm and the shape of every engagement: scope, cadence,
            and the measurable outcome we are accountable for. Keeps ambitious
            technical work pointed at what the client actually needs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link founders-note" href="/about/">More about the firm</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band closing ground-blue">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="statement">Tell us what is at stake.</h2>
      <div class="closing-row">
        <p>
          Send a few honest sentences. You will hear back from Dan, usually
          within a business day, with a straight answer about whether we can help.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" data-contact-dialog class="button button-solid">
          Start a conversation
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
